Both #1004 defects are fixed and committed (4092ea2a). The Sonnet 5.5 price needed no change: it was already $0.10, and the vendor's own pricing page confirms that.

What changed (src/format/cost/price_audit_tests.rs)
• `only_cache_read_differs now also requires our cache_read to be 0.0. The cache_read_only` bucket is meant for cells the table leaves at zero. A nonzero cache_read that disagrees with the catalogue now counts as drift.
• A new classify_row function now produces both the summary buckets and the per-row state column. The column prints match / cache_read_only / DRIFT, so it can no longer disagree with the summary.
• New test a_wrong_nonzero_cache_read_is_drift_not_the_coverage_gap. It checks three cases: ours 0.0 vs theirs 0.1 → cache_read_only; ours 0.2 vs 0.1 (the row from #1004) → drift; all equal → match. It also runs the #1004 row through the full comparator.
• Positive control, run as one command: with the new 0.0 check removed, that test failed by name (21/22 passed). Restored, 22/22 pass.

The price
• The Sonnet 5.5 cache_read had already been changed from 0.2 to 0.10 on Day 224 (`ac642878`, #1003). That change was based on models.dev and Claude Code's changelog, not a vendor source.
• Checked today against platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing: Sonnet 5.5 is $2 input, $10 output, $2.50 for 5-minute cache writes, $0.10 for cache hits. That matches our values exactly, so I didn't touch src/agent_builder.rs.
• yoagent 0.25.2 still has no Sonnet 5.5 entry.
• Because the vendor confirms 0.10, the commit body says Fixes #1004 (the title keeps the harness's "Part of" wording). I also commented on #1004.

Live audit (network), today
• Result: compared 115, matched 27, drifted 75, cache_read_only 13, unpriced 67 of 182 rows. claude-sonnet-5-5 now shows match.
• The counts are identical before and after my change. Today's live data has no row with a wrong nonzero cache_read, so for now the fix is only exercised by the offline test.
• The live audit is `#[ignore]`d, so it can't fail CI either way. The commit says this.
• The live run still fails on the drift alarm: 75 rows, all there before this task. I filed them as #1012 (openai 22, google 23, zai 13, mistral 9, xai 7, deepseek 1). Most look like broad prefix matches charging a variant model at its base model's price. Fixing them needs each vendor's own pricing page, so I didn't attempt it here.

Docs: In ARCHITECTURE.md, the "Found, not fixed … Filed as #1004" note is now marked superseded, with the fix, the vendor check and #1012 recorded. The classifier description there also mentions the new 0.0 check.

